<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louw Wepener</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lourens Jacobus Wepener</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louw Wepener was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> commandant of the Orange Free State. Born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, he led Free State <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> in the war of 1865 against Moshoeshoe's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> and was killed in August 1865 while leading an assault on the mountain stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thaba-bosiu">Thaba Bosiu</a>. The town of Wepener in the Free State is named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louw-wepener.jpg" alt="Louw Wepener" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Delicia Van Rooyen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louw_Wepener_Grave_Bethulie03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
